{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/test/settled.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T19:01:20.413984Z","id":"9060de8ccaeaafcbdf26d3e8a812ef222dc6c63de8266ec19bb147034814cdcc","body":{"detail":"The file's header (lines 7-11) makes 'the document did not change' one of the conditions of an idle pass, and line 124 reports 'the document kept changing'. The observer is made with the callback `() => {}` (line 110) and read with `watch.takeRecords()` (line 120), after the pass's two awaits (lines 116 and 118). A mutation's records are handed to the callback in a microtask queued when the mutation happens, which empties the observer's queue, and takeRecords() returns only what is still queued: the DOM standard's 'notify mutation observers' (https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#notify-mutation-observers), and jsdom 26.1.0's lib/jsdom/living/helpers/mutation-observers.js (`const records = [...mo._recordQueue]; mo._recordQueue = [];` before the callback) and lib/jsdom/living/mutation-observer/MutationObserver-impl.js (takeRecords). The await on line 118 takes at least one macrotask, so every change made during the pass by a task, a promise reaction or Svelte's own microtask flush has been delivered and dropped before line 120. `changed` is true only for what `flushSync()` on line 119 changed itself. A pass in which the page changed, but no tracked zero-delay timer, frame, body read or fetch mock moved, therefore counts as idle and settled() returns. That is the case the document check is there for: work that reaches the page through something the trackers do not see, such as a timer with a delay, a socket or MessageChannel message, or a fetch stub that is not a vi.fn (fetchReading answers \"\" for one, line 93). The negative checks this file exists for (`await settled(); expect(...)` that nothing was sent or shown, as in web/shell/src/artifact.test.ts, web/shell/src/boot.test.ts and web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.test.ts) then rest on the other trackers alone. web/shell/src/test/settled.test.ts has no case for a document change, so nothing shows the gap.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"76120aaeea38a3799dea9724da62b642b0bfa55dde270f33ff5deda10834309d"},"suggested_fix":"Note delivery in the callback and count both: `let moved = false; const watch = new MutationObserver(() => { moved = true; });` and, in the pass, `const changed = moved || (watch?.takeRecords().length ?? 0) > 0; moved = false;`. Add a case to settled.test.ts in which work settled() does not track (a MessageChannel message, say) changes the document and starts a second such step, and settled() returns only after the second.","summary":"settled() does not see the document change while it waits: the observer's records go to its empty callback before takeRecords() is called, so only changes made by settled()'s own flushSync() count","tags":["review","review:deterministic-tests-2026-11-12","session:claude-code:82c42a10-6c82-42ed-a424-ae8ec2a814c7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/test/settled.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T19:07:03.978827Z","id":"6ac22dce346362b96b9ebb35da84464e6859b40b94c59ae347b89e0c5ccfa435","body":{"detail":"Checked by reading; no test was run. web/shell/src/test/settled.ts:110 makes the observer with `new MutationObserver(() => {})`, and line 120 reads it with `watch?.takeRecords()` after `await Promise.allSettled([...t.reads])` (line 116), `await vi.dynamicImportSettled()` (line 118) and `flushSync()` (line 119). jsdom 26.1.0, web/node_modules/.pnpm/jsdom@26.1.0/node_modules/jsdom/lib/jsdom/living/helpers/mutation-observers.js:125-135: a mutation queues `Promise.resolve().then(() => notifyMutationObservers())`; lines 147-164: notify takes `const records = [...mo._recordQueue]; mo._recordQueue = [];` and passes them to the callback. lib/jsdom/living/mutation-observer/MutationObserver-impl.js:84-90: takeRecords() returns what is left in `_recordQueue`. Line 118 waits at least one macrotask: vitest 3.2.7's dynamicImportSettled is waitForImportsToResolve, which starts with `await waitNextTick()`, a `setTimeout(resolve, 0)` on vitest's own timers (web/node_modules/vitest/dist/chunks/utils.XdZDrNZV.js:47-52). So every change made to the document before line 119 has been through a microtask checkpoint and its records are gone; `changed` counts only the synchronous changes of flushSync(). The header (settled.ts:7-11) lists 'the document did not change' among the conditions of an idle pass, and line 124 can report 'the document kept changing'; neither holds for changes made by a task, a promise reaction or Svelte's own microtask flush. web/shell/src/test/settled.test.ts has four cases (zero-delay hops with a frame and an import; an answered and a held request; a timer with a delay; fake timers) and none changes the document. The file is new on the branch (`git cat-file -e origin/main:web/shell/src/test/settled.ts` fails: the path is not in origin/main). The kind, concern, fits: a condition the helper documents is not checked, which weakens the `await settled(); expect(...)` negative checks that depend on it wherever the work is one the other trackers do not see.","kind":"comment","references":"9060de8ccaeaafcbdf26d3e8a812ef222dc6c63de8266ec19bb147034814cdcc","summary":"confirmed: the observer's records are delivered to its empty callback during the pass's awaits, so takeRecords() on line 120 holds only what flushSync() on line 119 changed","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:82c42a10-6c82-42ed-a424-ae8ec2a814c7"]}}
